      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x-2}-2?$",
      "worked_solution": "To obtain the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x-2}-2,$ we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph to the right by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x-2}.$\n\n- Translate the result down by $2$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x-2}-2.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14258624/assets/737440e358ea4f8373f211250142546c6739de1dfc3d6db6ee0f4b7e83204972.png)",
